% Insurance eligibility (LPS2's rule base, as valid DRL)
%
% The Logical English (for LPS) twin of a Drools rule base, written by the DRL translator
% from LPS2's reading of insurance.drl (kept in sources/).
% Each Drools rule is a reactive rule. Its facts are states of the world, and what it does to
% working memory (insert, modify, delete) is something happening in the world, with its causal law.

the target language is: lps.

the maximum time is 10.

the actions are:
    the band of the policy for *a driver* becomes *a band*; known as policy_band_becomes.
    a policy starts for *a driver* with band *a band*; known as policy_starts.

the fluents are:
    there is a driver called *a name* with age *an age* and record *a record*; known as driver.
    there is a policy for *a driver* with band *a band*; known as policy.

the knowledge base insurance includes:

the text of the rule base is at "sources/insurance.drl".

% Rule "young drivers are high risk"
if there is a driver called a name with age young and record a record
    and it is not the case that there is a policy for the name with band a band
then a policy starts for the name with band high.

when a policy starts for a driver with band high
then there is a policy for the driver with band high.

% Rule "a clean record over thirty is low risk"
if there is a driver called a name with age mature and record clean
    and it is not the case that there is a policy for the name with band a band
then a policy starts for the name with band low.

when a policy starts for a driver with band low
then there is a policy for the driver with band low.

% Rule "a claim moves a low band to standard"
if there is a driver called a name with age an age and record claimed
    and there is a policy for the name with band low
then the band of the policy for the name becomes standard.

when the band of the policy for a driver becomes standard
then there is a policy for the driver with band standard
    and it is not the case that there is a policy for the driver with band low.

initially there is a driver called ann with age young and record clean
    and there is a driver called bob with age mature and record clean
    and there is a driver called cid with age mature and record claimed
    and there is a policy for cid with band low.

% Drools (a KieSession on the same working memory and steps) fired 3 rule(s) and ended with
% (its facts as this twin's fluents):
%   - policy(ann,high)
%   - policy(bob,low)
%   - policy(cid,standard)
%   - driver(ann,young,clean)
%   - driver(bob,mature,clean)
%   - driver(cid,mature,claimed)
% The twin's final state under LPS2 (`lps state`) is compared with it by test_drools.pl.
